tPascalIdeal -- give the Pascal ideal of t-spread monomials of a given polynomial ring
**************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        tPascalIdeal(S,t)
  * Inputs:
      * S, a polynomial ring
      * t, a positive integer that identifies the t-spread contest
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the Pascal ideal of t-spread
        monomials of S

Description
===========

the function tPascalIdeal(S,t) returns the Pascal ideal of t-spread monomials
of S, that is, the ideal generated by the minimum number of t-spread monomials
of S with the greatest possible degrees and such that the supports of the
generators are pairwise disjoint.

Examples:

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : S=QQ[x_1..x_10]                    |
|                                        |
|o1 = S                                  |
|                                        |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                     |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : tPascalIdeal(S,3)                  |
|                                        |
|o2 = ideal (x x x x  , x x x , x x x )  |
|             1 4 7 10   2 5 8   3 6 9   |
|                                        |
|o2 : Ideal of S                         |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : tPascalIdeal(S,4)                  |
|                                        |
|o3 = ideal (x x x , x x x  , x x , x x )|
|             1 5 9   2 6 10   3 7   4 8 |
|                                        |
|o3 : Ideal of S                         |
+----------------------------------------+

Ways to use tPascalIdeal:
=========================

  * "tPascalIdeal(Ring,ZZ)"

