MaxInd -- optional integer argument for tLastMon
************************************************

Description
===========

whether it is greater than -1 the function tLastMon(u,t,MaxInd=>m) gives the
smallest t-spread monomial for which the maximum of the support is
$\max\textrm{supp}(\texttt{u})$ of the Borel shadow of
$B_\texttt{t}\{\texttt{u}\}$. Given a $t$-spread monomial
$u=x_{i_1}x_{i_2}\cdots x_{i_d}$, we define $\textrm{supp}(u)=\{i_1,i_2,\ldots,
i_d\}$.

See also
========

  * *note tLastMon: tLastMon, -- give the last t-spread monomial of the Borel
    shadow a given t-spread monomial
  * *note tShadow: tShadow, -- give the t-spread shadow of a given t-spread
    monomial or a given list of t-spread monomials

